msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:131
msgid "Set the maximum number of images allowed in each folder. Leave empty for the default of 30. A membership plan can raise or lower this per plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:138
msgid "Videos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:139
msgid "Allow uploading videos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:145
msgid "Likes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:146
msgid "Let visitors like individual photos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:147
msgid "Adds a heart button to every photo, with a count everyone can see. Only signed-in visitors can like, and each person can like a photo once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:154
msgid "AI Moderation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:155
msgid "Review the first ten photos in each folder with AI"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:156
msgid "Checks a folder's photos with OpenAI when the vendor saves the folder, using the API key from the HivePress Integrations settings. The first ten photos in the folder are checked together in one free request; any beyond the tenth are not checked. OpenAI fetches each photo from your site, so this only covers public folders: photos in private and members-only folders are skipped while Protect Files is on, because their files are not served at a public address. Your site must also be publicly reachable, so on local or private sites, and whenever the service is unavailable, saving simply proceeds unchecked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:162
msgid "Comments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:163
msgid "Let visitors comment on individual photos"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:164
msgid "Every photo gets its own page with a comment thread beneath it, where signed-in visitors can comment, reply and like comments. People can delete their own comments, and the folder owner can delete any comment on their photos."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:171
msgid "Protect Files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:172
msgid "Protect private and members-only image files"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:173
msgid "Moves the files in private and members-only folders out of the folder your web server publishes, and serves them through an access-checked link instead, so there is no direct address to open. New uploads also get unguessable file names, and gallery images are excluded from public media API results. Recommended. If the files cannot be moved out on your hosting, a notice above says so and explains what to do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:180
msgid "Button Corner Rounding (px)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:181
msgid "Rounds the corners of every button this plugin adds, so they match the rest of your site. Leave it empty and each button keeps whatever shape your theme gives it, which is right on most sites. Set 0 for square corners, or a larger number for rounder ones."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:189
msgid "Maximum File Size (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:190
msgid "Reject gallery uploads larger than this many megabytes. Leave empty for no gallery-specific limit (the server upload limit still applies)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:197
msgid "Storage Limit (MB)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:198
msgid "Cap the total disk space each vendor's gallery may use, counting every photo and its thumbnails. Vendors see their usage on their Gallery page. Leave empty for no cap. A membership plan can raise or lower this per plan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:205
msgid "Allowed Image Formats"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:206
msgid "Choose which image formats vendors may upload. Leave empty to allow all supported formats."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:220
msgid "Maximum Image Dimensions (pixels)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:221
msgid "Resize uploaded images so their width and height do not exceed this many pixels. Photos straight from a phone or camera are far bigger than any screen needs, so this is the single biggest saving; around 2000 suits most galleries. Leave empty to keep the original dimensions. For compression, WebP conversion and bulk work on images you already have, use a dedicated image plugin alongside this one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:230
msgid "Gallery Monetisation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:231
msgid "Members-only folders are how galleries make money: visitors must unlock them before seeing inside. <strong>To charge through memberships</strong>, add the gallery privileges to a paid HivePress Memberships plan, or add them to a free plan to simply require an account. <strong>To let vendors charge instead</strong>, enable paid access below: a locked folder then offers that vendor's one-off purchase, and only vendors who have not set a price fall back to your upgrade page link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:236
msgid "Members-Only Folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:237
msgid "Let vendors mark folders as members-only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:238
msgid "Members-only folders appear locked until a visitor gains access through a membership plan or a purchase. With this off, vendors only choose between public and private, and any existing members-only folders behave as private. Turn it off if your site has no plans to monetise galleries."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:245
msgid "Locked Folder Display"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:246
msgid "Choose how members-only folders appear to visitors without access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:252
msgid "Show blurred previews"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:253
msgid "Show locked placeholders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:254
msgid "Hide completely"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:259
msgid "Paid Access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:260
msgid "Let vendors sell access to their members-only folders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:261
msgid "Each vendor sets their own lengths and prices on their Gallery page, choosing from a day, a week, a month, three months or permanent access, and may offer up to three of them at once. Setting any is optional. Buying is a normal WooCommerce checkout and the unlock applies to that one vendor's locked folders. While a vendor sells access, their locked folders show the purchase button rather than the upgrade page link. Requires WooCommerce. With HivePress Marketplace active, these sales count towards vendor earnings and your usual commission applies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:267
msgid "Commission Rate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:268
msgid "Your percentage of a gallery access sale. Leave both commission boxes empty to take none. The amount is added on top at checkout and shown to the buyer as a separate line called Platform fee, so the vendor still receives the price they set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:277
msgid "Commission Fee"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:278
msgid "A flat amount on top of the rate, charged once per gallery access sale. Use either box on its own or both together."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:285
msgid "Upgrade Page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:286
msgid "Choose the page locked visitors are sent to, e.g. your membership pricing page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:296
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:297
msgid "Your galleries are kept if you ever delete this plugin. WordPress shows its own warning saying that deleting a plugin also deletes its data, but that warning is generic: it appears for every plugin and does not describe what this one does. Nothing below is removed unless you tick the box first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:302
msgid "Delete All Data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:303
msgid "Delete folders, likes, comments and settings when this plugin is deleted (photos stay in your media library)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/configs/settings.php:304
msgid "Leave this unticked, and deleting the plugin keeps every gallery folder, photo, like, comment, purchased access and setting, so reinstalling brings your galleries back exactly as they were. Tick it, and deleting the plugin permanently removes all of that. Photos themselves always stay in your media library either way. This cannot be undone, so only tick it if you are sure you are finished with the gallery."
msgstr ""

